          "text": "Freight - International Council on Clean Transportation Donate Press Room About About the ICCT Our Approach Vision 2050 Board of Directors Staff Locations Equity at the ICCT Financials Careers Publications Short Reads Staff Blog Market Spotlight Data Explorer Regions & Transport Regions Brazil China Europe India Mexico United States & Canada Africa & Middle East Asia & Pacific Latin America Global Cities Transport Light vehicles Heavy vehicles Aviation Maritime shipping Fuels Freight Non-road Tools for Policy & Research EV Monitor: Trucks & Buses The EV Advantage U.S. TCO Calculator Unpacking the role of SAFs Electrifying non-road EU Vehicle Market Statistics All policy & research tools Resource Library Browse by Topic Charts & Visualizations Videos Explainers Events Partnerships Donate Press room About Our Approach Vision 2050 Board of Directors Staff Locations Equity at the ICCT Financials Careers Search Search for: Freight Global freight activity is on track to quadruple by 2050. That makes the total freight transit system an important target for overhaul as heavy-duty vehicles account for disproportionate shares of fuel consumption, greenhouse gas emissions, and air pollution. Technological advances alone won’t do the job, so the ICCT’s Green Freight program takes a systems approach that includes advanced technologies and measures to shift freight to the most sustainable modes while optimizing supply chains. Subscribe to our Newsletter Latest Publications MORE Report Electrifying on-road freight in China: A meta-analysis of use cases July 31, 2026 Working Paper Electrifying on-road freight: A case study of tractor-trailer deployment by a beverage company in Guangdong Province July 1, 2026 Report Toward Greener Freight: The Intermodal Freight Supply Chain of a Chinese Automotive Manufacturer May 19, 2026 Report Toward greener freight: Best practice and future opportunity for decarbonizing the freight supply chain of Lenovo December 27, 2025 Staff blog MORE Beyond roads: Inland shipping is China’s next electrification frontier June 30, 2026 Beyond trucks: China’s low-carbon multimodal freight transition June 1, 2026 Mapping the Charge: Why Grid Data Is Key to Electrifying Road Freight November 26, 2025 Events MORE Conference 2026 Non-Road Electrification Summit 8 September 2026 Conference Off-Road and Freight Decarbonization Symposium 2025 8 September 2025 Webinar Are we ready to transition to zero-emission trucking? Road freight decarbonization in Europe 19 October 2022 Explainers MORE Video The pollutant and greenhouse gas implications of LNG trucks Infographic Toward greener supply chains Video Greening global supply chains, explained Researchers Yunyang Tang , Intern (Beijing) Rachel Muncrief , Interim CEO (Washington, DC) Hui He , China Managing Director (San Francisco) Uwe Tietge , Research Lead (Berlin) Oscar Delgado , Heavy-Duty Vehicles Program Director, Latin America and India (Washington, DC) Leticia Pineda , Mexico and Canada Regional Lead (San Francisco) Xiaoli Mao , Program Lead (Washington, D.C.) Join our mailing list to keep up with ICCT’s latest research and analysis. Twitter YouTube LinkedIn Bluesky Contact Us &copy; 2026 International Council on Clean Transportation. All Rights Reserved. Privacy Policy / Legal / Sitemap / Web Development by Boxcar Studio We use cookies to improve site functionality and make this website more useful to visitors. Find out more . Accept Reject Settings Privacy Overview Essential Cookies Analytics Privacy Overview This website uses cookies to enable some basic functionality and also to help us understand how visitors use the site, so that we can improve it. Essential Cookies Essential cookies provide basic core functionality, such as saving user preferences. You can disable these cookies in your browser settings. Enable or Disable Cookies Enabled Disabled Analytics We use Google Analytics to collect anonymous information about how visitors interact with this