          "url": "https://www.intercargo.org/sulphur-cap-2020-guidance-and-useful-info/",
          "text": "2020 Sulphur Limit - Guidance and useful information - Intercargo --> ✕ CONTACT US MEMBER LOGIN SEARCH HOME ABOUT US EVENTS & FORUMS COMMITTEES TOPICS REGULATIONS NEWS & UPDATES RESOURCES MEMBERSHIP CONTACT US MEMBER LOGIN SEARCH NEWS & UPDATES 2020 Sulphur Limit - Guidance and useful information Tue 26 Nov The global limit of of 0.5% sulphur in ships’ fuel oil (the Sulphur Cap) has been adopted and approved by the International Maritime Organisation (IMO) and will enter into force on the 01 January 2020. In addition to the Sulphur Cap, the IMO adopted amendments to MARPOL Annex VI which will ban carriage of non-compliant fuel for use by ships (the carriage ban). You need to log in to view this content. Related Resources IMO INTERCARGO pre-brief for ISWG-GHG 22 August 25, 2026 EU Regulations Noticeboard Technical Committee INTERCARGO's Technical Updates for 2026 July 18, 2026 IMO In Focus Noticeboard INTERCARGO’s Briefs for IMO’s MEPC 84 May 1, 2026 IMO In Focus Noticeboard INTERCARGO’s Briefs for IMO’s ISWG-GHG 21 April 9, 2026 IMO Noticeboard Other Legislation INTERCARGO's Pre-Brief for IMO FAL 50 March 17, 2026 IMO Noticeboard Other Legislation INTERCARGO’s Pre-Brief for IMO SSE 12 March 6, 2026 Address 1st floor, 8-9 Northumberland Street London WC2N 5DA, United Kingdom Phone +44 (0) 20 8106 8480 Email info@intercargo.org Quick Links About Us Join Us Constitution Antitrust Careers Recent News Dry bulk trade and fleet updates 2026 September 3, 2026 Joint Industry Statement : Shipping industry welcomes the proposed inclusion of Indian ship recycling yards on the European List September 2, 2026 Advice for Members regarding situation in Strait of Hormuz and Middle East September 1, 2026 Selected News Headlines August 28, 2026 Follow Us --> Privacy Policy © 2026 Intercargo. All rights reserved. Design & Development by Tychetech"
