 of your interests and show you relevant adverts on other sites. They do not store directly personal information, but are based on uniquely identifying your browser and internet device. If you do not allow these cookies, you will experience less targeted advertising. Enhanced Conversions : If you agree, we may process limited information you provide (such as an email address) to better measure the effectiveness of our campaigns. The information is hashed before transmission and used only for measurement. If you decline, no Enhanced Conversions data will be processed. If you consent to the relevant cookie category (e.g., Performance/Measurement and/or Personalization, depending on our consent settings), we use “Enhanced Conversions” to improve the accuracy of marketing conversion measurement and attribution. When you complete certain actions on our website (e.g., submitting a form, requesting a quote, registering), we may use limited first party information you provide (such as email address or phone number) to help measure whether a campaign led to a conversion. Before any transfer, this information is hashed using a one way cryptographic transformation (i.e., converted into a pseudonymous value). The hashed value may be shared with our analytics/advertising partners (e.g., Google) and used solely to improve conversion matching and reporting, particularly in cases where browser settings limit traditional cookie-based measurement. Your choices matter : If you do not consent, or if you later withdraw consent, we will not process or transmit this data for Enhanced Conversions, and related tracking will be blocked/restricted accordingly. You can update your preferences anytime via the cookie settings link on our website. We aim to process only the minimum data necessary for measurement and do not intentionally send sensitive information. For more information, please refer to the Cookie Policy. For California Residents For California Residents The California Consumer Privacy Act (CCPA) Laws in California have changed to provide consumers with more transparency and options. As of January 1, 2020, California residents can request a report of their data and how it has been used, opt-out of the sale of data, or request data deletion. To opt out of the use of data at a browser level, you can choose not to allow advertising cookies on the Advertising Cookies tab. To opt out of offline sales of data, click on ”Submit data request” below and follow the prompts. Submit data request Back Button Cookie List Filter Button Consent Leg.Interest checkbox label label checkbox label label checkbox label label Clear checkbox label label Apply Cancel Confirm My Choices Select All"
