          "md": "| Date | Event | Status |\n|---|---|---|\n| 2012 | EU ETS first applied to aviation sector in Europe. *Source: European Commission, undated.* | In force |\n| 2021–2023 | CORSIA Pilot Phase (voluntary). *Source: ICAO CORSIA homepage, undated.* | Completed |\n| 2024 | CORSIA First Phase begins (voluntary state participation). *Source: GreenAir News, 18 December 2025.* | In force |\n| January 2025 | EU non-CO₂ aviation MRV system begins applying. *Source: European Commission, undated.* | In force |\n| 2024 | EU ETS free allocation to aircraft operators reduced by 25%. Full auctioning moves to 2026. *Source: European Commission, undated.* | In force |\n| 2025 | EU ETS free allocation to aircraft operators reduced by 50%. *Source: European Commission, undated.* | In force |\n| 19 November 2025 | ICAO Council approves classification of new feedstocks and default core LCA values for CORSIA eligible fuels. *Source: ICAO CORSIA Eligible Fuels page, November 2025.* | Completed |\n| December 2025 | ICAO releases 2024 Sector's Growth Factor (0.15405257); governments begin informing airlines of Phase 1 offsetting requirements. *Source: GreenAir News, 18 December 2025.* | Completed |\n| March 2026 | First large-scale Phase 1 CORSIA credit retirement by a commercial airline (Japan Airlines, via Shell, 180,000 Gold Standard credits). *Source: Gold Standard, 24 March 2026.* | Completed |\n| 2026 | EU ETS full auctioning in effect for aviation. *Source: European Commission, undated.* | In force |\n| By July 2026 | European Commission assessment of whether EU ETS scope should extend to international departing flights. *Source: European Commission, undated.* | Pending |\n| 2024–2026 | CORSIA First Phase continues. Airlines accumulating Phase 1 offsetting obligations. *Source: GreenAir News, 18 December 2025.* | In force |\n| January 2027 | Earliest start of EU ETS full scope extension (subject to July 2026 assessment outcome). *Source: European Commission, undated.* | Conditional |\n| 2027 | CORSIA Second Phase begins. Gold Standard and Verra approved as EEU suppliers for this phase. *Source: GreenAir News, 18 December 2025.* | Upcoming |\n| January 2028 | Phase 1 compliance deadline: airlines cancel EEUs for 2024–2026 offsetting obligations. *Source: Gold Standard, 24 March 2026.* | Upcoming — PRIMARY DEADLINE |\n| End of 2027 | European Commission delivers report on non-CO₂ aviation MRV results; may trigger legislative proposal. *Source: European Commission, undated.* | Upcoming |\n| 2027–2029 | CORSIA Second Phase. *Source: GreenAir News, 18 December 2025.* | Upcoming |\n| 2029–2035 | CORSIA Third Phase (mandatory, broader participation). *Analytical inference:* IATA's projection of \"nearly 2 billion EEUs through to 2035\" implies Third Phase obligations continuing. *Source: GreenAir News, 18 December 2025.* | Forward |\n\n---"
