          "text": "Prioritizing Energy Efficiency | Better Buildings & Better Plants Initiative Skip to main content Better Buildings & Better Plants Initiative Solutions Energy Efficiency Water & Waste Utilization and Storage Workforce Development Financing Navigator Programs & Partners Better Buildings Challenge Better Plants Challenge Partner List Sectors More Ways to Participate Initiative Partners Accelerators Home Energy Score Water Savings Network Waste Reduction Network Working Groups 50001 Energy Management Systems Onsite Energy Technology Campaigns Technology Research Teams Residential Network Leadership Goal Achievers Better Project & Better Practice Awards Financial Innovation Awards SWAP Events & Webinars Summit Events & Webinars Calendar Webinar Series On-Demand Webinars E-Learning Center Newsroom Just Added Announcements & Press Releases Annual Reports Beat Blog The Bulletin Better Buildings & Better Plants: Partners in the News Subscribe Join Prioritizing Energy Efficiency Energy-efficient facilities use less energy to provide the same level of occupant comfort, and energy-efficient manufacturing facilities use less energy to produce the same goods. Prioritizing energy efficiency is among the easiest and most cost-effective ways to reduce energy use, making it the ideal first step to enhancing operational efficiency and creating reliable infrastructure. Through the Better Buildings Challenge, DOE works with diverse partners to share their successes in adopting energy-efficient processes and technologies. Efficient Processes Learn how energy-efficient processes can help ensure that buildings and plants operate smoothly and efficiently. Efficient Technologies Explore highly efficient technologies that can help reduce costs in buildings and plants. Featured Resources Better Buildings Challenge Saving Energy: A Quick Start Guide for Small to Medium Manufacturers Energy Intensity Baselining and Tracking Guidance Published on: 01/02/2024 ABOUT Footer subme