          "section_id": "bf316ef0-ddf8-4309-b5e0-1bb060e3af1b",
          "key": "1",
          "md": "This document synthesises publicly available primary and corroborating source material on the United Arab Emirates' National Hydrogen Strategy and its surrounding regulatory framework, with specific attention to implications for logistics and freight forwarding operations. It covers the strategy's headline targets, implementation architecture, supporting regulatory instruments, and the current status of enacted versus draft provisions.\n\n**Convention notes:**\n- FACT claims are drawn verbatim from the SOURCE blocks provided in the corpus. Every FACT carries an inline source citation.\n- ANALYSIS claims are labeled *Analytical inference:*, *Industry interpretation:*, or *Operational implication:* per the provenance contract.\n- Items requiring legal determination carry *Legal Confirmation Required:* callouts.\n- The workspace is referenced by operational role, never by name.\n- Four source blocks are available in the corpus; all four are drawn upon.\n- **Critical provenance note:** No enacted legislative decree titled \"UAE National Hydrogen Strategy Implementation Decree for Logistics\" exists in the source corpus. The corpus contains the UAE National Hydrogen Strategy (published July 2023), supporting policy frameworks, and legal commentary. This brief is produced on the basis of the actual sourced content. Where a specific figure, deadline, or provision is not present in the corpus, an explicit GAP statement is emitted.\n\n---"
