        {
          "section_id": "d14fef4a-c471-4235-9bc9-80bb1729137b",
          "key": "10",
          "md": "*Specific [registration or reporting obligations] for logistics or freight forwarding operators under the UAE National Hydrogen Strategy are not available from primary sources as of June 2025.*\n\nFACT: The strategy's ten key implementation areas include \"policy, regulation and standards\" and \"finance and investments,\" each with implementation plans running through to 2031. *Source: CMS Expert Guide to Hydrogen – United Arab Emirates, CMS Law, 11 Feb 2025. https://cms.law/en/int/expert-guides/cms-expert-guide-to-hydrogen/united-arab-emirates. These pillars are expected to generate subordinate reporting instruments, but none have been enacted and identified in the corpus.\n\n*Operational implication:* Workspaces handling cargo for UAE industrial clients subject to EU carbon border adjustment mechanisms should confirm with those clients whether low-carbon logistics documentation (emissions per tonne-kilometre, fuel type, carrier certificates) is required to support client reporting under EU instruments — this is a client-driven requirement, not a direct UAE hydrogen strategy obligation.\n\n---"
        },
