          "key": "8",
          "md": "## National-Level Targets (Framework Layer)\n\n**FACT:** The UAE's economy-wide net zero target is 2050. The nearest interim milestone is the 2030 NDC emissions reduction target. *Source: Climate Action Tracker, UAE Policies and Action, 15 November 2024. https://climateactiontracker.org/countries/uae/policies-action/\n\n**FACT:** \"The CAT estimates the UAE's 2030 emissions under current policies are set, in a best case scenario, to plateau close to 2022 levels, at around 214 MtCO2e, or continue to increase to about 259 MtCO2e.\" *Source: Climate Action Tracker, UAE Policies and Action, 15 November 2024. https://climateactiontracker.org/countries/uae/policies-action/\n\n*Analytical inference:* \"Under current policies, the UAE is set to miss its latest 2030 emissions reduction target. To meet its 2030 NDC target, the government needs to implement more ambitious policies and reduce its 2030 emissions by a further 15–40%.\" *Source: Climate Action Tracker, UAE Policies and Action, 15 November 2024. https://climateactiontracker.org/countries/uae/policies-action/\n\n*Analytical inference:* A 15–40% gap between current-policy trajectory and the 2030 NDC target creates strong policy pressure for additional implementing instruments across all sectors, including transport, before 2030.\n\n## Transport Sector Energy Strategy Requirements\n\n*Analytical inference:* The UAE's energy strategy sets a target \"to produce at least 30% of its electricity through renewable sources by 2030.\" *Source: Climate Action Tracker, UAE Policies and Action, 15 November 2024. https://climateactiontracker.org/countries/uae/policies-action/\n\n*Analytical inference:* The UAE plans to reach \"19.8 GW of renewables installed capacity in 2030, with an expected 33 TWh of generation, up from 6 GW of total installed capacity in 2023.\" *Source: Climate Action Tracker, UAE Policies and Action, 15 November 2024. https://climateactiontracker.org/countries/uae/policies-action/\n\n**FACT:** The UAE's LTS sets a grid coefficient target of \"0.27 tCO2e/MWh, a 51% reduction from the 2019 baseline level of 0.55 tCO2e/MWh\" by 2030. *Source: Climate Action Tracker, UAE Policies and Action, 15 November 2024. https://climateactiontracker.org/countries/uae/policies-action/\n\n*Operational implication:* Logistics facilities and EV charging infrastructure in the UAE operating on grid power will see their Scope 2 emissions factor fall by approximately half between 2019 and 2030 if the UAE meets this target, which directly improves the emissions profile of electrified warehouse and road operations.\n\n## Fossil Fuel Investment Trajectory — Qualification\n\n**FACT:** \"The UAE is planning to significantly increase its oil production in the next years, and is pushing to reach 'gas self-sufficiency', with major investments in offshore gas production. In November 2022, ADNOC announced a USD 150bn investment plan to expand its oil and gas business in the next five years.\" *Source: Climate Action Tracker, UAE Policies and Action, 15 November 2024. https://climateactiontracker.org/countries/uae/policies-action/\n\n*Analytical inference:* Continued fossil fuel investment at this scale indicates that UAE domestic fuel prices for diesel and gas are unlikely to see policy-driven rapid increases in the near term, which reduces short-term cost pressure on road freight operators but also reduces the economic incentive to transition to alternative fuels absent a regulatory mandate.\n\n## Per-Year Trajectory — Power Sector (Relevant to Transport Electrification)\n\n*Analytical inference:* Nuclear energy accounted for 20% of UAE electricity generation in 2023, renewables 8%, and fossil gas 72%. *Source: Climate Action Tracker, UAE Policies and Action, 15 November 2024. https://climateactiontracker.org/countries/uae/policies-action/\n\n*Analytical inference:* The UAE's 2050 target is \"a zero-emissions grid coefficient.\" The LTS projects this is \"expected to rely heavily on the use of CCS on gas power plants, instead of a plan to phase out fossil fuels from power generation.\" *Source: Climate Action Tracker, UAE Policies and Action, 15 November 2024. https://climateactiontracker.org/countries/uae/policies-action/\n\n*The full per-year trajectory of transport-sector sub-targets (e.g., fleet electrification percentages, road freight fuel mandates, aviation SAF blending targets year-by-year) is not available from primary corpus sources as of 6 June 2026.*\n\n---"
