          "md": "The following milestones are grounded in the corpus. Where dates are confirmed by source, they are labeled FACT. Where they are framework commitments rather than enacted deadlines, this is noted.\n\n| Milestone | Date | Status | Source |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| UAE Net Zero 2050 announced | 2021 | In force (as national commitment) | CAT |\n| UAE NDC update submitted | 2023 | In force | CAT |\n| UAE LTS published (UNFCCC submission) | Early 2024 | In force | CAT |\n| UAE Energy Strategy 2050 (updated version) | 2023 | In force | CAT |\n| Renewables: 30% of electricity by 2030 | 2030 | Target | CAT |\n| Renewables installed capacity: 19.8 GW | 2030 | Target | CAT |\n| Grid coefficient: 0.27 tCO2e/MWh (−51% vs 2019) | 2030 | Target | CAT |\n| Power sector emissions: ~68 MtCO2e | 2030 | NDC sectoral target | CAT |\n| UAE overall NDC emissions reduction target | 2030 | Target (15–40% gap vs current policies) | CAT |\n| CCS deployment for power and industry | Post-2030 | Planned (heavy reliance) | CAT |\n| Grid coefficient: zero-emissions | 2050 | National net zero target | CAT |\n\n*Analytical inference:* \"The UAE's LTS, published in 2024, includes targets and current policy projections for all major sectors of the economy.\" *Source: Climate Action Tracker, UAE Policies and Action, 15 November 2024. https://climateactiontracker.org/countries/uae/policies-action/\n\n*Analytical inference:* *Specific enacted implementing deadlines for transport-sector operators (fleet standards, fuel mandates, reporting obligations) with fixed legal compliance dates are not available from primary corpus sources as of 6 June 2026.*\n\n---"
