          "md": "### Q1: Is the UAE Net Zero 2050 Transport Roadmap a binding legislative instrument?\n\n**Decided (from corpus):** The UAE Net Zero 2050 initiative is a national strategic framework. The LTS and NDC are policy documents submitted to the UNFCCC. Binding obligations on private sector operators flow from implementing legislation at federal or emirate level. *Source: Climate Action Tracker, UAE Policies and Action, 15 November 2024. https://climateactiontracker.org/countries/uae/policies-action/\n\n### Q2: Does the transport sector target apply to freight operations, or only passenger transport?\n\n*Specific scope definition from the transport sector provisions of the LTS is not available from primary corpus sources as of 6 June 2026.* The CAT references transport as a covered sector without disaggregating freight from passenger. *Legal Confirmation Required:* Whether freight forwarding and logistics operations fall within the defined transport sector scope of any specific implementing instrument requires review of that instrument's definitions.\n\n### Q3: Does the workspace's role as freight forwarder (rather than transport operator) affect its compliance exposure?\n\n*Legal Confirmation Required:* The distinction between a freight forwarder (as organiser of transport) and a carrier (as direct operator) is legally determinative for most transport-sector obligations. This determination requires legal review of the specific implementing instrument.\n\n### Q4: Do UAE Free Zone operations (e.g., Jebel Ali, Dubai South) fall within the initiative's scope?\n\n*Specific treatment of free zones under transport-sector implementing instruments is not available from primary corpus sources as of 6 June 2026.* Free zones have historically had distinct regulatory treatment in the UAE. *Legal Confirmation Required:* Whether free zone logistics operations are within scope requires legal review of each implementing instrument.\n\n---"
