        {
          "section_id": "c85b39b3-0689-4820-84c3-d94de34b41e4",
          "key": "7",
          "md": "**MONITORING — re-check window: Q1 2026 (NYK charter delivery tracking) and Q4 2025 (Air Products–Yara FID announcement)**\n\n*Analytical inference:* The earliest point at which ammonia-fueled vessel capacity appears to enter commercial time-charter service, based on the corroborator metadata, is November 2026 (NYK AFMGC delivery). This is for a medium gas carrier, not a container vessel. *Analytical inference:* Container-lane deployment of ammonia propulsion, based on industry-standard vessel development timelines, is more likely to reach commercial scale in the 2028–2031 window, coinciding with the FuelEU Maritime tightening schedule and IMO 2030 GHG intensity targets.\n\n**Specific actions for the workspace:**\n\n1. **Brief ocean carrier account managers now** — ask for their ammonia-vessel delivery pipeline and FuelEU Maritime compliance strategy. This is a relationship-building and data-access move, not a procurement decision. Carrier conversations initiated in 2025–2026 are the prerequisite for data-sharing agreements when ammonia-fueled capacity goes live.\n\n2. **Track the Air Products–Yara FID announcement** — if and when a final investment decision is taken on the Louisiana Clean Energy Complex or NEOM supply, it confirms long-run supply certainty that underpins carrier fleet investment. This converts the supply signal to a planning input.\n\n3. **Monitor the NYK AFMGC delivery in Q4 2026** — this is the first concrete data point on ammonia vessel commercial readiness. The charter structure (well-to-wake carbon intensity terms, data reporting obligations) will set precedents for subsequent charters and for forwarder contract language.\n\n4. **Add ammonia fuel transition as a standing agenda item in annual carrier sustainability reviews** — specifically request FuelEU Maritime compliance pathway documentation and well-to-wake methodology commitments. This creates the audit trail needed for Scope 3 Category 4 reporting if ammonia-fueled legs become available.\n\n5. **Do not commit to client-facing ammonia green lane claims before 2027** — the infrastructure pipeline does not support credible claims before that window, and premature claims create greenwashing exposure under EU Green Claims Directive enforcement timelines.\n\n*Analytical inference:* The re-check window for this brief is Q1 2026. By that point, the Air Products–Yara FID status should be public, the NYK delivery is within a 12-month horizon, and the FuelEU Maritime first compliance year (2025) will have generated initial carrier reporting data. A regeneration at that point will carry materially more operational specificity.\n\n---\n\n## New Sources Identified\n\n| Source Name | URL | Tier estimate (1-7) | Why this source matters |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Yara Clean Ammonia – Official Hub Page | https://www.yara.com/yara-clean-ammonia/ | 2 | Primary operator source for fleet size (15 ships, 18 terminals), strategy, and latest news; essential for span-grounding fleet and terminal FACT claims on next retrieval. |\n| Air Products & Yara Advanced Negotiations on Low-emission Ammonia Projects | https://www.airproducts.com/company/news-center/2025/12/1208-air-products-and-yara-advanced-negotiations-on-low-emission-ammonia-projects | 2 | Official Air Products press release (Dec 2025) covering Louisiana Clean Energy Complex and NEOM; 2.8 Mt/yr offtake and 25-yr structure; FID target; currently blocked (403) — retrieval retry required. |\n| Yara Clean Ammonia & NYK – World's First Time-Charter for Ammonia-Fueled MGC | https://www.yara.com/corporate-releases/yara-clean-ammonia-and-nyk-conclude-worlds-first-time-charter-agreement-for-ammonia-fueled-medium-gas-carrier/ | 2 | Details world's first AFMGC time-charter (YCA + NYK, delivery Nov 2026); required for span-grounding the charter delivery date and well-to-wake compliance framing. |\n| Yara Drives Hydrogen Economy with New Ammonia Import Terminal (Brunsbüttel) | https://www.yara.com/corporate-releases/yara-drives-hydrogen-economy-with-new-ammonia-import-terminal/ | 2 | Covers Oct 2024 opening of Brunsbüttel terminal: 3 Mt/yr import capacity, ~5% of EU 2030 hydrogen target; required for span-grounding European import infrastructure FACT claims. |\n| Ammonia Energy Association – Yara Organisation Profile | https://ammoniaenergy.org/organization/yara/ | 4 | Independent aggregator of Yara's full project portfolio (Sluiskil CCS, MOL charters, bunkering pilots, AM Green, ACME deals); useful for editorial cross-check and timeline verification. |\n| Yara Clean Ammonia Supports Groundbreaking Ammonia Bunkering Pilot in Pilbara | https://www.yara.com/corporate-releases/yara-clean-ammonia-supports-groundbreaking-ammonia-bunkering-pilot-in-pilbara/ | 2 | June 2025 press release on world's first STS ammonia bunkering transfer at anchorage (Port Dampier, WA) with GCMD; required for span-grounding bunkering pilot FACT claims and Asia-Pacific corridor relevance. |\n\n---"
