          "url": "https://ammoniaenergy.org/certification/pilot/",
          "text": "AEA Ammonia Certification System — Pilot Phase - Ammonia Energy Association AEA Ammonia Certification System — Pilot Phase - Ammonia Energy Association /* IE 9 and lower only */ /* END IE 9 and lower only */ skip to main content MENU LEAD Certification Pilot Registry Auditors Documents Articles Webinars Conferences 2026 Annual Conference Presentations Membership Register as an Industry Member AEA Membership Directory Sign up for our Newsletter Member Login About AEA Leadership AEA Staff Ammonia-Energy-Association-Logo-Horizontal-Color Search Ammonia-Energy-Association-Logo-Horizontal-Color LEAD Certification Pilot Registry Auditors Documents Articles Webinars Conferences 2026 Annual Conference Presentations Membership Register as an Industry Member AEA Membership Directory Sign up for our Newsletter Member Login About AEA Leadership AEA Staff Search AEA Ammonia Certification System — Pilot Phase Pilot operation of the AEA Ammonia Certification System began in September 2025 and remains open to all entities in the ammonia value chain, including producers, traders and distributors, and consumers. Participation is open to both members and non-members of the AEA. Early pilot participants are now preparing their initial audits, before the first certificates can be generated. While the full list of participants is not public, the following organizations have chosen to announce their participation: Envision Energy (China) NH3 Clean Energy (Australia) Pilot Objectives The objective of the pilot is to operate the AEA Ammonia Certification System in a live environment, making improvements based on practical experience of pilot participants, and identifying upgrades and expansions for full-scale implementation. The pilot will be a success if it can enable an account holder to generate, transfer and retire certificates ; that display environmental attribute(s) generated using an approved methodology ; from a plant that has undergone a certified audit by a qualified auditor ; with accurate life cycle information stored in a secure registry . Join the Certification Pilot today! To join the pilot, please contact us at certification@ammoniaenergy.org . You may wish to review the following documents: Pilot Participation Agreement System Documentation Pilot Overview (how it works, timeline, costs, and how to join). Interested parties that are not directly participating in the ammonia value chain but seek to understand the AEA Ammonia Certification System and its potential alignment with other market and regulatory frameworks (non-profits, government agencies, intergovernmental organizations) are also welcome to inquire about joining the pilot as an observer. In April 2026, we announced the pilot launch with a joint statement with AEA Ammonia Registry operator MiQ: To scale up and speed up the adoption of clean ammonia, market participants need high quality and credible data – rigorous accounting of actual carbon footprints – but we also need interoperability with different systems, to help align the requirements of voluntary and compliance markets across multiple sectors and countries. Our pilot participants will be demonstrating this in the year ahead, including participating plants in the Americas, Europe, and Asia-Pacific, which will be using various pathways, including electrolysis, natural gas with CCS, and other technologies to supply certified ammonia to consumers in multiple sectors. Trevor Brown, AEA Executive Director, quoted in AEA’s pilot launch announcement (April 27, 2026) For any additional questions, please contact certification@ammoniaenergy.org . Annual Conference Registration Now Open Join the AEA's Ammonia Certification System Download the LEAD Datasets Get the Newsletter Register here for the AEA’s weekly round-up of the global ammonia energy news. Featured Items --> Latest Articles Electric Hydrogen to supply electrolysers in Karratha, Western Australia Ammobia and Lummus partner to licence and deploy new ammonia production technology Azane, Equinor sign ammonia fuel supply agreement Mitsui E&S commercializes marine ammonia engine Construction begins on Blue Point project Ammonia-Energy-Association-Logo-Horizontal-Color Ammonia Energy Association 44927 George Washington Blvd, Suite 265 Ashburn, VA 20147 USA Quick Links LEAD Certification Pilot Registry Auditors Documents Articles Webinars Conferences 2026 Annual Conference Presentations Membership Register as an Industry Member AEA Membership Directory Sign up for our Newsletter Member Login About AEA Leadership AEA Staff Copyright © 2026 Ammonia Energy Association. All Rights Reserved. Site designed and developed by Social Ink"
