        {
          "section_id": "c744b31e-5403-4e7b-a55c-f63c44b0a962",
          "key": "14",
          "md": "| Date | Event | Status |\n|---|---|---|\n| **2019** | Metro Council passes Renewable Energy Standards legislation establishing phased carbon-free energy targets for Metro Government | In force |\n| **November 2020** | Metro Council adopts building code upgrade to 2018 International Building Codes (commercial zEPI: 49.5) | In force |\n| **2022** | Metro Government benchmarks 335 facilities across 20.3M sq ft; total energy: ~1.3B kBTUs | Completed |\n| **2023** | Nashville adopts C-PACER program for commercial energy efficiency financing | In force |\n| **2026 (expected)** | 40 MW TVA Green Invest solar farm near Tullahoma operational; accounts for ~13% of Metro annual power supply | Pending |\n| **2041** | 100% total carbon-free energy resources target for Metro Government under RPS | Future target |\n| **TBD** | Commercial benchmarking ordinance for private buildings — stakeholder input phase as of ACEEE update (September 2023) | Pre-adoption; re-check Q4 2026 |\n\n**Effective date:** The RPS was passed in 2019 and is in force. The 2018 IBC building code upgrade was adopted November 2020 and is in force. *Source: Sustainability (Mayor's Office), Metro Nashville; Nashville City Scorecard, ACEEE.*\n\n**Primary deadline:** 100% carbon-free energy for Metro Government by 2041, with annual stairstep targets. Specific annual percentages not available from primary sources as of May 2026. *Source: Energy Sustainability in Metro Nashville Government, General Services.*\n\n**Jurisdictional scope:** Metropolitan Government of Nashville and Davidson County. *Source: Metro Government Energy Benchmarking, General Services.*\n\n**Penalty summary:** Specific financial penalty provisions not available from primary sources as of May 2026. *Legal Confirmation Required:* enforcement mechanisms and penalty exposure for non-compliance with existing Metro building energy programs require legal review of the enacted ordinance text.\n\n---"
